{
  "title": "Ignore review progress notifications when waiting for actionable feedback",
  "description": "The PR watcher treats any new non-author comment as review feedback and exits with code 2.\n\
On PR #48, the Codex connector posted a comment marked <!-- codex-pull-request-review-summary --> whose only status was Code Review: Running, and agent-submit stopped with instructions to address the comments even though there were no findings or inline comments.\n\
Distinguish review progress notifications from actionable review feedback so agent-submit continues watching until the review finishes or actual findings arrive.\n\
Preserve real review comments, inline feedback, and completed review outcomes.\n\
Add regression tests for the connector progress comment and for genuine feedback arriving afterward.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
